35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems our budget is tighter than expected, and our revenue depends heavily on where the care is delivered.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Interesting. It seems some of our past trials actually worked, yet they were simply abandoned. A waste of potential, wouldn't you say?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found that our nursing vacancies are quite high, though the midwifery team seems to have some breathing room. We must be careful.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh boy, we have a problem! The parking is full by eleven and the booking system is missing a lot of the actual work being done.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I see. It seems we have a habit of starting things with a smile, but forgetting to agree on who will hold the umbrella when it rains.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, if the booking system is unreliable, we might be underestimating the actual cost of running a new program.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, ""forgetting"" is a polite word for it. We lack a logical follow-through. We should prioritize a program that addresses a proven need.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I agree. If we add more work to the ward nurses who are already stretched, we might cause more harm than good.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's what I'm worried about! If we add a new program, will the rooms just overflow? We can't just squeeze more in.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Let us be gentle with our staff. If a program relies on an outside body or a shared rota, we must ensure they are truly happy to help.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, a ""proven need"" is only useful if the regional fund actually pays for it. We cannot afford a deficit next year.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, a deficit is a temporary financial state. A failure to treat patients because we abandoned a working system is a permanent failure of logic.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I feel we should look for a program that utilizes the areas where we have capacity, like midwifery, rather than the wards.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just want to make sure that whatever we pick doesn't make the shuttle buses stop running or the parking lot a disaster zone!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is so important to listen to everyone. I worry that if we pick something too complex, it will simply break once the excitement fades.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
